    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "York Harbor was first settled by Europeans in 1624, though Native Americans had lived there long before.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://southernmainecoast.com/york-maine/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The waterfront area known as Lower Town was renamed York Harbor during a municipal upgrade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/York_Harbor%2C_Maine",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nathaniel Grant Marshall bought the slum of Stage Neck in 1871, razed shacks, and built the 325‑guest Marshall House.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/York_Harbor%2C_Maine",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "York Harbor became a Gilded Age summer colony famed for its resort architecture and Shingle‑style mansions built 1880‑1890.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/York_Harbor%2C_Maine",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Marshalls also founded York Harbor & Beach Railroad, which opened in 1887 and linked the town to the broader region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/York_Harbor%2C_Maine",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A ferry licensed in 1652 crossed from the high‑tide island of Gallows Point to Seabury, connecting York Harbor to the mainland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
